# Free LLM providers — generated from registry.yaml, do not edit by hand.
# Fill the keys you use, then `source` this file. Every endpoint is
# OpenAI-compatible: point any SDK/agent at the base URL next to the key.

# ── Google AI Studio (Gemini API) — base: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/ · get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
export GOOGLE_AI_STUDIO_API_KEY=""
#    note: pass the key as Bearer

# ── opencode — base: https://opencode.ai/zen/v1 · get a key: https://opencode.ai/auth
export OPENCODE_API_KEY=""
#    note: these are the six ids Zen prices at zero; inside an opencode config the same id is written opencode/<model-id>. Every other id on the same base URL is metered. The catalog also still returns deepseek-v4-flash-free and laguna-s-2.1-free, which the pricing table stopped listing at zero — treat them as metered until it says otherwise

# ── OpenRouter (free models) — base: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 · get a key: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=""
#    note: pick models with the :free suffix; the five suffixed ids were zero-priced on 2026-08-11. openrouter/free is different in kind — the catalog calls it the Free Models Router, prices it 0/0 and lets it pick whichever free model is up, so it is the id that survives this lane rotating (confirmed 2026-08-14). It is a router, not a coding model, which is why it is here and not in the column

# ── Groq — base: https://api.groq.com/openai/v1 · get a key: https://console.groq.com/keys
export GROQ_API_KEY=""
#    note: the ids Groq's own Free Plan Limits table names

# ── Kilo Code — base: https://api.kilo.ai/api/gateway · get a key: https://app.kilo.ai/profile
export KILO_CODE_API_KEY=""
#    note: every id listed is priced 0 — the same catalog meters 346 more. kilo-auto/free and openrouter/free are routers, and nemotron-3.5-content-safety is a guardrail classifier, so none of the three is a coding model. The lane rotates fast — Ling 3.0 Flash left it in 2026-08, ling-3.0-tiny:free stood in its place for three days and was gone by 2026-08-14, with liquid/lfm-2.5-2.6b:free arriving instead — which is why the ids that come and go stay here and out of the Models column

# ── Requesty — base: https://router.requesty.ai/v1 · get a key: https://app.requesty.ai/api-keys
export REQUESTY_API_KEY=""
#    note: the ten ids listed are every row the catalog prices at 0, and the free plan serves those alone — ids here carry no :free suffix, so the price is the only thing separating them from the 585 metered rows beside them. nemotron-3.5-content-safety is a guardrail classifier rather than a coding model

# ── AIHubMix (free models) — base: https://aihubmix.com/v1 · get a key: https://aihubmix.com/token
export AIHUBMIX_API_KEY=""
#    note: the ten ids listed are the coding-relevant half of the 49 rows the catalog priced at 0 on 2026-08-14. The proprietary ones beside them (gpt-5.5-free, gpt-4.1-free, gemini-3.7-flash-free) are the platform paying for inference it resells, so they rotate faster than the open-weight rows and are deliberately not listed here. `model_id` is the callable string; `model_name` in the same catalog is a display title

# ── Z.ai (Zhipu GLM) — base: https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4 · get a key: https://z.ai/manage-apikey/apikey-list
export ZAI_GLM_API_KEY=""
#    note: Coding-Plan keys use https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4 instead

# ── Cerebras Inference — base: https://api.cerebras.ai/v1 · get a key: https://cloud.cerebras.ai
export CEREBRAS_API_KEY=""
#    note: the Free Trial tier reaches every model in the public catalog, which is these two: "Every model on the public Model Catalog is available on the Free Trial tier, subject to the per-model Free Trial rate limits"

# ── Cloudflare Workers AI — base: https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/ai/v1 · get a key: https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
export CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_API_KEY=""
#    note: substitute {account_id} with your Cloudflare account ID

# ── Routeway — base: https://api.routeway.ai/v1 · get a key: https://routeway.ai/dashboard/keys
export ROUTEWAY_API_KEY=""
#    note: all ten ids are priced 0 and answering — the Free-models column names the four the probe anchors on, because a promo lane that rotates out must not archive a gateway that still has a free tier; laguna-m.1:free is priced 0 too but the catalog still marks it unavailable, so it is left out, and ling-3.0-flash:free left the catalog altogether in 2026-08. Only the :free suffix is zero-priced — the same catalog meters Claude and GPT at list rates. The gateway publishes no legal entity or terms of service and supports users through Discord alone, so treat these ids as a fallback lane, not a dependency

# ── SambaNova Cloud — base: https://api.sambanova.ai/v1 · get a key: https://cloud.sambanova.ai/apis
export SAMBANOVA_CLOUD_API_KEY=""
#    note: model ids are case-sensitive; the catalog publishes list prices for every row, so the free tier is a quota rather than a zero-priced lane

# ── Vercel AI Gateway — base: https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1 · get a key: https://vercel.com/dashboard/ai-gateway/api-keys
export VERCEL_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=""
#    note: this id costs nothing; any other Free-Tier-eligible model spends the $5 monthly credit. zai/glm-4.6v-flash was the second one until it left the catalog by the 2026-08-20 read. inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-free left in 2026-08 too, and the ling-3.0-tiny-free standing where it was publishes an empty pricing object, so nothing there says it is free

# ── Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (DashScope, international) — base: https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1 · get a key: https://modelstudio.console.alibabacloud.com
export ALIBABA_MODEL_STUDIO_API_KEY=""
#    note: international (Singapore) endpoint; keys are region-specific

# ── BazaarLink — base: https://api.bazaarlink.ai/v1 · get a key: https://bazaarlink.ai/keys
export BAZAARLINK_API_KEY=""
#    note: only the :free id and auto:free cost nothing — the plain qwen3.7-flash beside it in the catalog is the metered twin ($0.03/$0.13 per 1M). auto:free picks a free model for you, and on a funded account it can fall through to the paid routing table "unless paid fallback is disabled"

# ── NVIDIA NIM (build.nvidia.com) — base: https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1 · get a key: https://build.nvidia.com
export NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=""
#    note: the catalog endpoint answers unauthenticated, which is what the probe reads — it confirms NVIDIA still hosts these models, not that your account still has credits to call them with

# ── TokenRouter (PaleBlueDot) — base: https://api.tokenrouter.com/v1 · get a key: https://www.tokenrouter.com/console/token
export TOKENROUTER_API_KEY=""
#    note: one id in the catalog is priced 0 and it is the whole free lane here. PaleBlueDot AI runs this gateway on tokenrouter.com; same-name gateways on other TLDs are separate services and their keys do not work here

# ── Cohere (trial keys) — base: https://api.cohere.com/compatibility/v1 · get a key: https://dashboard.cohere.com/api-keys
export COHERE_API_KEY=""
#    note: OpenAI-compatible endpoint; native API lives at https://api.cohere.com/v2. Both ids are the Model ID Cohere's own model pages publish — north-mini-code-1-0 is the free-on-any-key one

# ── Hugging Face Inference Providers — base: https://router.huggingface.co/v1 · get a key: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
export HUGGINGFACE_INFERENCE_API_KEY=""
#    note: chat-only; model ids namespaced (openai/gpt-oss-120b)

# ── OVHcloud AI Endpoints — no key needed · base: https://oai.endpoints.kepler.ai.cloud.ovh.net/v1
#    note: no key at all on the anonymous lane, which OVHcloud rate-limits at 2 requests per minute per IP per model — a 429 means wait about half a minute, not that the offer is gone. An API access key from a Public Cloud project raises that to 400 per minute and bills per token from then on

# ── Upstage (Solar API) — base: https://api.upstage.ai/v1 · get a key: https://console.upstage.ai/api-keys
export UPSTAGE_API_KEY=""

# ── SEA-LION (AI Singapore) — base: https://api.sea-lion.ai/v1 · get a key: https://playground.sea-lion.ai/key-manager
export SEA_LION_API_KEY=""
#    note: the key manager calls it a Trial API Key but publishes no expiry and no credit balance — the documented ceiling is the 10 calls/min rate limit. /v1/models needs the key, so the probe reads the offer page

# ── SenseNova (SenseTime 商汤) — base: https://token.sensenova.cn/v1 · get a key: https://platform.sensenova.cn
export SENSENOVA_API_KEY=""
#    note: the base url is not printed on any server-rendered page — it is taken from the vendor's console docs and corroborated directly, since token.sensenova.cn/v1/models answers 401 "Authorization Not Found" in an OpenAI-shaped envelope. The callable ids live only in that JavaScript console, which no probe here can read, so none are published; the plan page names "SenseNova 6.8 Flash Lite" in prose alone. Beware sensenova-6.7-flash-lite, which third-party lists still carry — the vendor routes it to 6.8 and retires the alias on 2026-08-31

# ── Inception Labs (Mercury) — base: https://api.inceptionlabs.ai/v1 · get a key: https://platform.inceptionlabs.ai
export INCEPTION_LABS_API_KEY=""
#    note: mercury-2 answers /v1/chat/completions; mercury-edit-2 answers /v1/fim/completions and /v1/edit/completions instead, so an OpenAI-shaped chat client cannot call it — point an autocomplete plugin at it, not a chat agent

# ── Pollinations.AI — no key needed · base: https://text.pollinations.ai/openai
#    note: anonymous works and needs no key. The optional token that raises the rate limit has no working signup — auth.pollinations.ai, the host the vendor's own APIDOCS still sends you to, stopped resolving (NXDOMAIN from both Cloudflare and Google resolvers, 2026-08-14)

